    "The proposed signage, by reason of its siting, appearance, and design would appear visually intrusive and incongruous within the street scene harming visual amenity, including the character and appearance of the host property and the character and appearance of the Central Richmond Conservation Area. There is no public benefit proposed to outweigh the harm. The scheme would be contrary to the NPPF and, in particular, policies 28 and 29 of the Local Plan, policy HC1 of the London Plan, the Shopfronts SPD and Richmond and Richmond Hill Village Planning Guidance as supported by the Central Richmond Conservation Area Statement and Central Richmond Conservation Area Appraisal."
